  description: A star is a massive, luminous sphere of extremely hot plasma held
    together by gravity. Stars generate energy through nuclear fusion in their cores,
    producing the light and heat that can influence the environments of surrounding
    planets.
  interestingFact: The Sun is the closest star to Earth, which is why it appears
    much brighter and larger than the stars seen at night.
